From cfd6b0a3d30192f6c361459c41e8b7626b7eb1b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: C0fuge <189659128+C0fuge@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 03:53:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libhdfs3: DIGEST-MD5 SASL client with auth-conf (step 1 of
 data-transfer SASL)

libgsasl's DIGEST-MD5 has no confidentiality: it refuses qop=auth-conf
(and gsasl_encode returns an error for it), so a DataNode with
dfs.data.transfer.protection=privacy cannot be read through it.

DigestMd5Client (src/rpc/DigestMd5Client.{h,cpp}, OpenSSL libcrypto only):
- RFC 2831 client: md5-sess, digest-uri protocol/serverName, charset
  utf-8, maxbuf, rspauth verified (mutual authentication)
- QOP auth / auth-int / auth-conf chosen from a client preference list
- auth-int: HMAC-MD5(Kic, seq || msg)[0..9] + type + seq, as the JDK
- auth-conf: 3des (CBC, EDE K1 K2 K1 with DES parity), des, rc4,
  rc4-56, rc4-40; key derivation, padding, chained cipher state and
  sequence numbers as the JDK's DigestMD5Base, which DataNodes use
- wrap / unwrap / maxRawSendSize for the stream layer

Not wired into the block reader yet (next: SASL handshake in
RemoteBlockReader and a wrapping Socket).
